{
 "id": "050-zeynepin-arkadasi-tasiniyor",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "Can's Friend Is Moving Away",
 "theme": "A friend moving away, saying goodbye",
 "blurb": "Can's best friend Deniz is moving to another city. Can sobs and sobs, talks with his mum about how crying can help too, and makes Deniz a box full of their shared memories.",
 "voiceNames": {
  "can": "Can",
  "deniz": "Deniz (Can's friend)",
  "anne": "Mum (Can's mum)"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "Can and Deniz lived on the same street. Every day they played ball together in the park. Boing, boing, the ball bounced! Tee-hee, they both giggled. “You're my best friend!” said Can.",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "You're my best friend!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "And you're mine!"
    },
    "top": {
     "say": "Boing, boing!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch the ball!",
   "ask": "Who is your best friend? What do you play together most?",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 22,
     "fx": "kahkaha"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "One evening Deniz hung her head. “We're moving to another city,” she said. Deniz was very sad too. A lump came into Can's throat. Drip, drip, drip… Tears rolled down his cheek.",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "But I'll miss you so much!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "I'm very sad too."
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Deniz!",
   "ask": "Why is Can crying? How do you think Deniz feels?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Can ran home. He sobbed and sobbed. “Mum, is it bad to cry?” Mum hugged him tight. “No, my love. We cry when we're sad. I cry when I miss someone too.” Can took a deep breath in through his nose. Then he let it out slowly: fffff…",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "Sniff… I'll miss her so much."
    },
    "anne": {
     "say": "Cry, my love, I'm right here."
    }
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "What do you think Can will do for Deniz?",
    "res": "Let's see!",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "Draw a picture"
     },
     {
      "l": "Make a present"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Touch Can!",
   "ask": "How does Can feel? What do you do when you're sad? Who do you hug?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Can had an idea. “Mum, shall we make Deniz a memory box?” Mum brought a box. Can drew a picture: two friends holding hands, and a heart. The ball they played with went in the box! And the book they read together!",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "The box was my idea!"
    },
    "anne": {
     "say": "What a lovely idea! I'll hold the ribbon."
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "The memory box is ready!",
    "msg": "All in the box!"
   },
   "hint": "Put the picture in the box!",
   "ask": "If you made a memory box for a friend, what would you put inside?"
  },
  {
   "text": "The next morning, Can and Mum went to Deniz's house. Step, step, one more step. Deniz was waiting at the door. When she saw the box, her eyes lit up: “That's our ball!”",
   "mech": {
    "say": "Step, step!",
    "done": "Can reached Deniz's house!"
   },
   "hits": {
    "deniz": {
     "say": "That's our ball!"
    },
    "anne": {
     "say": "Slowly, slowly, we walk on the pavement."
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Can to make him walk!",
   "ask": "How did Deniz feel when she saw the box? Look at her face. How can you tell?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Deniz held out a kite for Can. “When you fly it, remember me!” The two friends hugged tight. They laughed a little, and they cried a little. Can felt sad and warm inside, both at once.",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "I'll never forget you!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "When you fly it, remember me!"
    },
    "anne": {
     "say": "What good friends you two are."
    },
    "kutu": {
     "say": "Ball, picture, book… all in here!"
    },
    "ucurtma": {
     "say": "Deniz's kite is Can's now!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Deniz!",
   "ask": "Why does Can feel sad and warm at the same time? Have you ever felt two feelings at once?"
  },
  {
   "text": "It was time. Deniz waved before she got into the car. “Bye-bye, Deniz!” called Can. “We'll video call tonight!” The kite sailed up into the sky, whoooo, whoooo. Can smiled. Tonight he would show Deniz the kite.",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "Bye-bye, Deniz! Talk tonight!"
    },
    "deniz": {
     "say": "Goodbye, Can! I'll call tonight!"
    },
    "anne": {
     "say": "We'll call together tonight, all right?"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Can!",
   "ask": "How can we talk to a friend who has moved far away? Who do you miss?",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 26,
     "fx": "ruzgar"
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "guide": {
  "kazanim": [
   "TADB.4 (learning outcome) Expressing their views on what they listen to or watch. Sub-outcome: says their feelings and thoughts about the material (tells which page of the story made them most sad or most happy, and why).",
   "TAKB.2 (learning outcome) Building the content of the speaking process. Sub-outcome: links the topic to prior knowledge and daily life (tells about their own experience with someone who moved away, lives far away or whom they miss).",
   "E2.1 Empathy: notices Can's and Deniz's sadness; says that the friend who is moving away is sad too.",
   "SDB3.2 Flexibility: sees ways of adapting to a situation they cannot change (a friend moving away): crying, hugging, making a memory box, planning a video call.",
   "D15 Love and D4 Friendship: experiences that love and friendship do not end with distance, and that the bond continues through video calls with a faraway friend."
  ],
  "once": [
   "Point to the two friends on the cover: “What do you think these two friends like to do?”",
   "Ask: “What does moving away mean? Have you ever moved, or do you know someone who has?”",
   "Children who have recently moved, been separated from a loved one or experienced a loss may have strong feelings during this story; do not push them to share, but give them the chance to talk if they want to."
  ],
  "sirasi": [
   "On page 2, at the sentence “Deniz was very sad too”, point to Deniz's face. While saying “Drip, drip, drip…”, show the tears rolling down the cheek with your fingers. Explain “a lump in his throat” by putting a hand to your throat.",
   "On page 3, repeat the question Can asks his mum: “Is it bad to cry?” Listen to the children's answers; speak in a way that accepts that everyone, girls and boys, big and small, may cry when they are sad. Take a deep breath in through your nose with Can, then let it out slowly: Fffff…",
   "On pages 5 and 6, look at Deniz's and Can's faces: “How are they feeling now? How can you tell?”"
  ],
  "sonra": [
   "Ask “What did Can do when he was sad?” and count together: he cried, hugged his mum, took a deep breath, made a memory box.",
   "Talk about the feeling of “sad and warm at once”: explain with examples that we can be sad and happy at the same time (when a holiday ends, when giving a friend a present).",
   "Give them the chance to say their view by asking “Which page of the story made you most sad, and which made you most happy? Why?” (TADB.4).",
   "Talk about how you keep in touch with loved ones who are far away: phone, video call, letters, sending pictures."
  ],
  "sinif": {
   "ad": "Memory Box",
   "sure": "20 min",
   "materyal": "Small cardboard boxes or a shoebox, paper, pastels, glue, ribbon",
   "adim": [
    "Make a circle. Each child tells about someone they miss or who lives far away: “I miss ..., because ...” (TAKB.2).",
    "With feeling cards (sad, happy, surprised), show Can's and Deniz's feelings in the story; the children explain: “Deniz was sad, because...”",
    "Each child draws a picture for someone they love and puts it in the box; they draw a game they played together or a memory.",
    "Tie the boxes with ribbon. Talk about how, when a friend moves away from the class, you could make them a memory box together as a class."
   ]
  },
  "evSoru": [
   "What did Can do when he was sad? What do you do when you're sad?",
   "Why was Deniz happy when she saw the box?",
   "Who do we miss who lives far away? How can we reach them?"
  ],
  "evEtk": {
   "ad": "Missing-You Letter",
   "d": "With your child, make a picture letter for a relative who lives far away, or make a video call. Your child shows their picture and tells them about a memory."
  },
  "aileNotu": "Today we read “Can's Friend Is Moving Away.” When his best friend moves away, Can is very sad; he cries and hears from his mum: “We cry when we're sad.” Then he makes a memory box for his friend. When your child cries, saying “You're very sad, I'm here” instead of “Don't cry” lets them feel that their feeling is accepted; this is the same for girls and boys. Video calling someone they miss or sending them a picture eases the pain of being apart. Children who have recently moved or been separated from a loved one may have strong feelings during this story; do not push them to share, but give them the chance to talk if they want to."
 },
